{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And HaShem will make you to abound.</b> He will grant you surpassing success beyond all prior success." "<b>For good — written in this book of the Torah.</b> As it says: וְהִתְהַלַּכְתִּי בְּתוֹכְכֶם וְהָיִיתִי לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי לְעָם (Leviticus 26:12). This He will do when He returns to rejoice over you for good because you obey — as He rejoiced over your fathers, not by merit of the fathers. This is because your return will be with all heart and all soul, so that your sins are accounted as merits, and you will be for a favor before Him as your fathers were."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {1 "The lemma combines two phrases from the verse; the second phrase 'written in this book of the Torah' is not present in the Masoretic text of Deut. 30:9 and likely reflects a variant reading or gloss in Sforno's text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:39.694394417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}